WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.630
Boosting begins with a prediction
and asks what it still misses.

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:10.650
For squared error, the next tree learns
observed target minus current prediction.

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:16.520
This sign is opposite to the prediction
minus target residual used by our scoring

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:17.450
functions.

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:20.730
Return to the four real training rows,

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.630
whose initial mean is
ninety four point two five.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:29.584
The two busy residuals are eighty four
point seven five and one hundred point

00:00:29.584 --> 00:00:30.330
seven five.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.590
Their mean is ninety two point seven five,

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.410
so the first busy leaf
stores a positive correction.

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:41.590
A target above the forecast
needs an upward move.

00:00:43.733 --> 00:00:49.183
We apply one tenth of that correction,
using learning rate zero point one.

00:00:49.613 --> 00:00:55.136
Ninety four point two five plus nine point
two seven five gives one hundred and three

00:00:55.136 --> 00:00:56.563
point five two five.

00:00:57.373 --> 00:01:02.973
The quiet branch has correction minus
ninety two point seven five and moves down

00:01:02.973 --> 00:01:04.963
to eighty four point nine seven five.

00:01:05.833 --> 00:01:08.563
These are deliberately partial moves.

00:01:08.913 --> 00:01:13.403
The first boosted prediction therefore
differs from the direct stump mean of one

00:01:13.403 --> 00:01:13.863
hundred and eighty seven.

00:01:15.413 --> 00:01:18.343
The rate controls the
contribution of a correction,

00:01:18.793 --> 00:01:22.603
while the stage count controls how
many successive corrections are fitted.

00:01:24.775 --> 00:01:26.385
After the first stage,

00:01:26.555 --> 00:01:29.865
the busy forecast is one hundred
and three point five two five.

00:01:30.555 --> 00:01:34.725
The remaining busy residual mean is
eighty three point four seven five,

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:38.205
not the original ninety
two point seven five.

00:01:39.175 --> 00:01:43.285
Applying one tenth of this new correction
gives one hundred and eleven point eight

00:01:43.285 --> 00:01:44.525
seven two five.

00:01:45.195 --> 00:01:49.285
This dependence on the running prediction
is what makes the fitting sequential.

00:01:50.115 --> 00:01:53.565
A forest instead averages
finished component forecasts.

00:01:54.515 --> 00:01:57.745
Our known answer checks
independently verify both stages,

00:01:58.015 --> 00:02:01.605
so the distinction is visible in
numbers as well as terminology.

00:02:03.983 --> 00:02:09.623
The snapshot replay starts with the saved
initial constant and adds each saved

00:02:09.623 --> 00:02:13.193
tree value multiplied by
the saved learning rate.

00:02:13.783 --> 00:02:17.933
These local names abbreviate the
actual snapshot fields in the source.

00:02:18.683 --> 00:02:22.873
Prediction performs no residual
fitting and receives no outcomes.

00:02:23.383 --> 00:02:26.073
The library constructed the
residual trees during training.

00:02:27.023 --> 00:02:32.593
Our full benchmark uses squared error,
depth three, leaf support ten,

00:02:33.163 --> 00:02:38.233
rate zero point one and one hundred,
two hundred or three hundred stages.

00:02:39.043 --> 00:02:41.193
Validation early stopping is disabled.

00:02:41.683 --> 00:02:44.593
The declared stage count,
together with the structural limits,

00:02:44.743 --> 00:02:46.673
is the actual stopping policy.

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:52.450
The full model starts at the
twenty eleven training mean,

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:55.170
about one hundred and forty
three point seven nine.

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:57.870
At the real busy Monday request,

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:03.046
its three hundred tree corrections sum to
about seven hundred and forty seven point

00:03:03.046 --> 00:03:04.050
three seven.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:08.717
Applying the rate gives a final forecast
of two hundred and eighteen point five

00:03:08.717 --> 00:03:09.310
three.

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:15.570
At two oclock, the same model instead
returns minus twenty five point five two.

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:20.260
Negative correction leaves can take the
total outside the nonnegative target

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:21.070
range.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:26.380
Our explicit clipping policy changes that
quiet forecast to zero and leaves the

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:28.490
positive busy forecast alone.

00:03:30.668 --> 00:03:35.768
Increasing the declared stage count lowers
training error and improves later error

00:03:35.768 --> 00:03:36.648
within this grid.

00:03:36.648 --> 00:03:42.538
Raw mean absolute error reaches about
one hundred and four point eight four;

00:03:43.188 --> 00:03:45.998
clipping reaches one hundred
and two point two two.

00:03:46.488 --> 00:03:50.138
Neither beats the grouped baseline
at ninety one point five seven.

00:03:50.528 --> 00:03:55.338
All three declared seeds give
identical scores in this setup.

00:03:55.728 --> 00:03:58.458
That is an observed
lack of variation here,

00:03:58.628 --> 00:04:00.998
not three independent future periods.

00:04:01.528 --> 00:04:05.058
A different learning rate or
loss would be another comparison.

00:04:06.028 --> 00:04:10.148
We retain the current settings and results
instead of silently enlarging the search

00:04:10.148 --> 00:04:11.398
after seeing them.

